      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've run into this issue as well, some additional details I've discovered:\n-the log spam only happens for remote clients. So if you sit in a spam chair you won't get any log errors locally but remote clients will see it (they may have to be late-joiner as well but I don't remember)\n-The amount of chairs that do it scales in some way to the amount of chairs in the world. If there's 100 chairs in the world then every chair seems to cause log spam. However at 60 chairs only some would cause log spam. Changing the number of chairs also changes which chairs cause log spam so it's very hard to nail-down.\nHere's a test world from when I was last testing it:\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_0e89b9f6-8b04-4d2c-9c7d-fbdf2e5a5a2b",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
